From 024764becb8ade60852f621290c2767f874afa2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:25:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): R6.2 - stable worker check, page lifecycle
 cancellation, verified cache cleanup

Incremental after baseline + R4 + R5 + R6 + R6.1. Draft; not deployed.
- staleWorkerGuard: evaluations are discarded if a controllerchange, a different controller
  or a different set of active workers is seen while they run (bounded retries, then
  blocked); stillCurrent() must hold immediately before the recovery tokens are used
- cache cleanup is verified (delete rejects/false/lies, listing fails, leftovers after a
  reload all block); only Cliniverse-owned legacy caches are ever deleted
- recoveryRun: page life cycle moved out of React; cancel prevents new guard side effects,
  fragment handling, history changes, recovery requests and UI updates after unmount or
  supersession (an update already sent still completes its global sign-out)
- blocked copy: 'This page did not use your recovery session.'
- tests: guard/run behavioural suite with mutations; Chromium scenarios for failed cache
  deletion and a previous-build negative control

